Z||000000||MooCow||07-24-2000||04:42 PM||||Okay every time I go to take off I hear a sliding like grinding noise behind me.  It only happens once in a while.  Does anyone know what this is.  My car is a 86 SE v6 4 speed with 130,734 on it.<P>                                Thanks Ken||||reg||5
Z||000001||Patrick||07-24-2000||05:24 PM||||<BR>Did ya raise the anchor?<P>Ken, in your first sentence you say "every time..." and then in your next sentence you say "It only happens once in a while". Which is it? It might make a difference in diagnosing the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000002||MooCow||07-24-2000||06:31 PM||||Oops sorry I mean it only happens once ina while whne I go to take off it makes that noise.  Anyone know y????<P>                                  Thanks Ken||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mattsfiero||07-25-2000||03:36 AM||||Every once in awhile.....hmmm....How are you with the clutch (Heavy or Easy). If you are too hard on the transmission you may have worn the gears in first and that could be the slipping you hear. Mine does it in third....Sometimes it's smooth sometimes it is ruff, I am guessing that the gear is going. The other thing to checkis your transmission Oil. It appears you have put some good miles on it  have you ever changed it?<P>Matt  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||07-25-2000||11:17 AM||||could be the throw out bearing... not releasing.<P>or<P>the bearing release arm...<P>or <P>a bad gear...<P>or <P>something with the master cylinder, not getting enough hydraulic pressure to the slave.<BR><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
